{"file": "D:\\SpaceBook\\Books\\6th\\Math\\JPG\\207.jpg", "lines": [{"text": "Introduction", "conf": 0.842, "box": [[201, 79], [452, 79], [452, 122], [201, 122]]}, {"text": "data and measure of central tendency.", "conf": 0.926, "box": [[249, 395], [838, 386], [838, 427], [250, 435]]}, {"text": "11.1Graphs", "conf": 0.891, "box": [[731, 524], [993, 517], [995, 568], [733, 575]]}, {"text": "Previous Knowledge Check", "conf": 0.896, "box": [[1158, 614], [1578, 625], [1577, 666], [1157, 654]]}, {"text": "Organising data in graphs gives us clear information and we", "conf": 0.931, "box": [[173, 643], [1099, 627], [1100, 674], [174, 691]]}, {"text": ".What is meant by data and", "conf": 0.878, "box": [[1168, 682], [1557, 694], [1556, 727], [1167, 715]]}, {"text": "can easily interpret and compare data. We know that a", "conf": 0.933, "box": [[174, 704], [1010, 691], [1011, 735], [175, 747]]}, {"text": "organization of data?", "conf": 0.889, "box": [[1202, 730], [1489, 732], [1488, 765], [1202, 763]]}, {"text": "picture graph, bar graph, line graph etc, are used to", "conf": 0.938, "box": [[175, 764], [967, 752], [967, 795], [176, 807]]}, {"text": "What isbargraph?How", "conf": 0.905, "box": [[1172, 770], [1523, 776], [1522, 810], [1172, 804]]}, {"text": "organise collected data. Now we will learn about drawing", "conf": 0.953, "box": [[176, 822], [1050, 813], [1051, 852], [177, 862]]}, {"text": "many types of bar graph?", "conf": 0.867, "box": [[1198, 814], [1540, 816], [1539, 853], [1198, 850]]}, {"text": "Howcanwe representdata", "conf": 0.892, "box": [[1172, 856], [1559, 862], [1558, 895], [1172, 890]]}, {"text": "bar graphs.", "conf": 0.838, "box": [[176, 881], [355, 881], [355, 921], [176, 921]]}, {"text": "by using bar graph?", "conf": 0.886, "box": [[1199, 900], [1468, 902], [1467, 936], [1199, 934]]}, {"text": "11.1.1MultipleBarGraph", "conf": 0.877, "box": [[179, 1018], [667, 1014], [668, 1054], [180, 1057]]}, {"text": "To organize categories of data, we usually use a bar chart. A bar graph or bar chart is", "conf": 0.943, "box": [[178, 1083], [1504, 1077], [1505, 1116], [179, 1122]]}, {"text": "represented by the height or length of bars of equal width. One bar of the graph represents", "conf": 0.936, "box": [[175, 1142], [1582, 1137], [1582, 1181], [176, 1186]]}, {"text": "one observation or quantity.", "conf": 0.896, "box": [[177, 1200], [616, 1204], [615, 1244], [176, 1240]]}, {"text": "Now we are going to learn how to draw and interpret a multiple bar graph. A multiple bar", "conf": 0.926, "box": [[174, 1260], [1562, 1256], [1562, 1309], [175, 1314]]}, {"text": "graph is an extension of simple bar graph. It shows the connection between different values", "conf": 0.929, "box": [[175, 1321], [1586, 1314], [1586, 1368], [176, 1374]]}, {"text": "of data. Each value is represented by a vertical or horizontal bar in the graph. Two or more", "conf": 0.949, "box": [[175, 1378], [1563, 1377], [1563, 1433], [175, 1434]]}, {"text": "distinguish categories of data.", "conf": 0.886, "box": [[187, 1567], [643, 1567], [643, 1603], [187, 1603]]}, {"text": "Drawinga Multiple Bar Chart", "conf": 0.85, "box": [[187, 1709], [662, 1709], [662, 1745], [187, 1745]]}, {"text": "distinguish between different categories.", "conf": 0.926, "box": [[184, 1886], [804, 1893], [803, 1944], [183, 1936]]}, {"text": "NOTFORSALE", "conf": 0.855, "box": [[277, 2070], [558, 2064], [559, 2097], [278, 2103]]}, {"text": "205", "conf": 0.749, "box": [[844, 2083], [915, 2083], [915, 2123], [844, 2123]]}]}